Compiled bundler runtime code, in test fixtures only
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Three fixtures under tests/fixtures/ are the output of a real local build, and so
each contains that bundler's own runtime loader (1.5-3.3 KB of loader glue per
fixture). The bundlers intend this code to ship inside application bundles. All
three are MIT licensed.

  tests/fixtures/webpack5-module-federation/
      webpack 5 jsonp chunk-loading and Module Federation runtime
      Copyright JS Foundation and other contributors
      MIT -- https://github.com/webpack/webpack

  tests/fixtures/metro-rn/
      metro-runtime module registry polyfill
      Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates
      MIT -- https://github.com/facebook/metro

  tests/fixtures/parcel-build/
      Parcel 2 parcelRequire loader and js/bundle-url/cache runtime modules
      Copyright (c) 2017-present Devon Govett and contributors
      MIT -- https://github.com/parcel-bundler/parcel

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reduced excerpts of public build manifests, in test fixtures only
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Three fixtures are minimal excerpts of PUBLIC build manifests, cut down to the few
lines a test needs, with hostnames replaced by reserved example domains. They are
route paths, key names and identifiers rather than program code.

  tests/fixtures/next-build-manifest/        shape of a Next.js Pages Router manifest
  tests/fixtures/remix-manifest/             shapes of a Remix v2 and a React Router v7 manifest

  The React Router website is MIT licensed:
      Copyright (c) React Training LLC 2015-2021, Shopify Inc. 2022-2025
      https://github.com/remix-run/react-router-website

